                          <div style="font-family: &quot;lato&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 28px;font-size: 18px; color: #333;"><strong>WHAT YOU NEED TO KNOW AS A NEW BOARD MEMBER</strong></div>
                          <div style="font-family: &quot;lato&quot;, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 28px;font-size: 16px; color: #333;">
                            First of all: did you receive Knowledge Transfer (KT) from the previous board?
                            Did you learn from them how to run your Local, what obligations you have towards AEGEE-Europe and what the tasks are of your board roles?
                            <br><br>
                            If the answer is NO, do not panic! Please, have a look at the
                            <a href="https://oms.aegee.org">KT Booklets</a>
                            and contact your NetCommie (your main contact person from AEGEE-Europe) as soon as possible, as they will be able to help you get further knowledge transfer.
                            Keep in mind that these booklets are general guidelines and that for specific details (bank account, social media passwords, local members etc.)
                            you need KT from the previous board.
                            <br><br>
                            <ul>
                              <li><a href="https://oms.aegee.org">Learn more about how to run a Local as a board</a> (to view the Knowledge Management System, click on login and log in via Google with your AEGEE GSuite account. See below how to request it);</li>
                              <li>Be aware, as an AEGEE Local, you have some obligations towards AEGEE-Europe called the <a href="https://my.aegee.eu/pages/antenna-criteria">Antenna Criteria</a>;</li>
                              <li>Keep in mind that after your term ends you have to transfer knowledge yourself. For that reason you can create your own knowledge transfer booklet for future generations, for which we have a <a href="https://oms.aegee.org">template here</a>.</li>
                            </ul>
